Z||000018||GT-maniac||08-29-2001||11:24 PM||||Well one thing you have to do is make sure you have the motor and cradle supported so as little weight as possible is on the bolts. I used a rented compressor and air ratchet to take the nuts off. Then after the usual copius amounts of WD40 I used an air chisel to drive the bolts out. You need the hammering action of the chisel to break the rust free. I used the chisel head and then a smaller bolt to push the cradle bolts out once they went past the inner hole. Not easy and I hope I never have to do it again but possible. You have bought new bolts for it I hope ?||||reg||1
